''nanas.''] '''1.''' A native name in tropical America of the pineapple, and of other plants resembling it. The wild ananas of the West Indies is ''Bromelia Pinguin.''—'''2.''' [''cap.''] [NL.] A small genus of tropical plants, belonging to the natural order ''Bromeliaceæ.'' ''A. sativa'' produces the pineapple. Also called ''Ananassa.''

