'''Ananchytinæ''' (an-ang-ki-tī′nē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Ananchytes'' + ''-inæ''.] A subfamily of sea-urchins, of the family ''Spatangidæ'', typified by the genus ''Ananchytes'', containing many fossil and a few surviving forms.

'''anandrous''' (an-an′drus), ''a.'' [< NL. ''anandrus'', < Gr. ἄνανδρος, without a man, < ἀν- priv. + ἀνήρ (ἀνδρ-), a man, a male, in mod. bot. a stamen.] In ''bot.'', without stamens: applied to female flowers. Also formerly applied to cryptogamic plants, because they were supposed to have no male organs.
